Dependencies are separate distributions. Their own licenses and notices continue
to apply; Cragkit's MIT declaration does not relicense them. Exact required and
optional versions are declared in each package manifest and the repository locks.
The Python core requires Pydantic; the Node core requires Zod. PostgreSQL clients,
HTTP clients, tokenizers, LangChain and MCP SDKs are installed only by the selected
profile or separate adapter package. Consult those installed distributions for
their license texts and transitive dependencies.

These Cragkit archives do not bundle database servers, model weights, model
runtimes or tokenizer rank assets. Supported server/profile names identify
compatibility, not a redistribution of those products. Tokenizer assets and local
model assets require explicit application setup and their applicable terms.

Hosted embedding and reranker profiles require an application-owned transport,
credential and disclosure policy. Cragkit supplies no built-in API key. Provider
service terms and usage charges are separate from the MIT license for this code.
No provider call or model download occurs merely by importing the core package.
